U panics the\nhypervisor. Non-protected guests and the host\u0027s own vCPUs are\nunaffected.\n\nUse hyp_panic() rather than BUG(): it reads unambiguously as a\ndeliberate crash to a reader unfamiliar with pKVM (where BUG()/WARN_ON()\nare both silently fatal at EL2), and it keeps checkpatch clean.\n\nThis is a deliberate fault for validating the CI pipeline: paired with\nthe tabba/ci-check-good branch, it must fail a protected-VM run while a\nnon-protected run still succeeds. Do not merge.\n\nBug: 538086469\nChange-Id: Id29b5d4ae1e43b6ff22c741db84bff3070267ef0\nSigned-off-by: Fuad Tabba \u003ctabba@google.com\u003e\n---\n\ndiff --git a/arch/arm64/kvm/hyp/nvhe/hyp-main.c b/arch/arm64/kvm/hyp/nvhe/hyp-main.c\nindex a552325..4314b62 100644\n--- a/arch/arm64/kvm/hyp/nvhe/hyp-main.c\n+++ b/arch/arm64/kvm/hyp/nvhe/hyp-main.c\n@@ -1038,6 +1038,15 @@ static void handle___kvm_vcpu_run(struct kvm_cpu_context *host_ctxt)\n \t\t\tgoto out;\n \t\t}\n \n+\t\t/*\n+\t\t * CI pipeline check (tabba/ci-check-bad): deliberately\n+\t\t * crash the hypervisor when running a protected vCPU, so a\n+\t\t * working CI MUST fail the protected-VM run. Non-protected\n+\t\t * guests and the host\u0027s own vCPUs are left untouched.\n+\t\t */\n+\t\tif (pkvm_hyp_vcpu_is_protected(hyp_vcpu))\n+\t\t\thyp_panic();\n+\n \t\tflush_hyp_vcpu(hyp_vcpu);\n \t\tret \u003d __kvm_vcpu_run(\u0026hyp_vcpu-\u003evcpu);\n \t\tsync_hyp_vcpu(hyp_vcpu, \u0026ret);\n\n\"\"\"\nIMPORTANT NOTE: Start directly with the output, do not output any delimiters.\nTake a Deep Breath, read the instructions again, read the inputs again. Each instruction is crucial and must be executed with utmost care and attention to detail.\n\nReview:",
